# The sdist ships the package and its metadata, not the test suite.
#
# setuptools-scm's file finder adds every git-tracked file under the project
# to the sdist, and tests/data/ is 31 MB of vendor measurement files. That is
# how the 0.0.18 sdist reached 11 MB against a 28 KB wheel — 417x the wheel,
# none of it code, carried by everyone who builds from source and stored on
# PyPI for ever, since a released file can be yanked but never replaced.
#
# Pruning all of tests/ rather than only tests/data/: the suite is built to
# fail, never skip, when a specimen is missing (tests/helpers/requirements.py
# — a run that passed without the real vendor files would report nothing).
# Shipping the tests without their data would therefore hand anyone who ran
# them a suite that fails by design. The tests live in git, which is where
# they are run from.
prune tests
